## Installation <a name="installation"></a>

### 1️⃣ Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/awesome-cli-productivity.git
cd awesome-cli-productivity
```

### 2️⃣ Source the script in your shell configuration

#### Bash (`~/.bashrc` or `~/.bash_profile`)

```bash
# Add this line at the end of your .bashrc
source "$HOME/awesome-cli-productivity/awesome.sh"
```

#### Zsh (`~/.zshrc`)

```zsh
# Add this line at the end of your .zshrc
source "$HOME/awesome-cli-productivity/awesome.sh"
```

### 3️⃣ Reload the shell

```bash
exec $SHELL -l   # or simply open a new terminal window
```

### 4️⃣ Verify installation

```bash
awesome_version
# Expected output: awesome-cli-productivity v1.0.0
```

