## Functions <a name="functions"></a>

Below are the core functions shipped with **awesome-cli-productivity**. All functions are defined in `awesome.sh` and are ready to use after sourcing.

### 1️⃣ `nodeinit <project_name> [--typescript]`

Bootstrap a Node.js (or TypeScript) project with sensible defaults.

```bash
nodeinit my-app               # creates folder, npm init -y, git init, .gitignore
nodeinit my-ts-app --typescript   # adds tsconfig.json, installs typescript
```

```bash
nodeinit() {
  local name=$1
  local ts_flag=$2
  if [[ -z "$name" ]]; then
    echo "Usage: nodeinit <project_name> [--typescript]"
    return 1
  fi
  mkdir -p "$name" && cd "$name" || return
  git init -q
  npm init -y >/dev/null
  npx license mit >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  cat > .gitignore <<'EOF'
node_modules
dist
.env
npm-debug.log
.DS_Store
EOF
  if [[ "$ts_flag" == "--typescript" ]]; then
    npm install -D typescript @types/node >/dev/null
    npx tsc --init --rootDir src --outDir dist --esModuleInterop >/dev/null
    mkdir -p src && echo "console.log('Hello, TypeScript!');" > src/index.ts
    echo "npm run build && node dist/index.js" > run.sh
    chmod +x run.sh
    echo "{
  \"scripts\": {
    \"build\": \"tsc\",
    \"start\": \"node dist/index.js\"
  }
}" > package.json
  else
    echo "console.log('Hello, Node!');" > index.js
  fi
  echo "✅ Project '$name' created."
}
```

