### 3️⃣ `goinit <module_name>`

Initialize a Go module with a basic project layout.

```bash
goinit github.com/user/project
```

```bash
goinit() {
  local mod=$1
  if [[ -z "$mod" ]]; then
    echo "Usage: goinit <module_path>"
    return 1
  fi
  mkdir -p "$(basename "$mod")" && cd "$(basename "$mod")" || return
  go mod init "$mod"
  mkdir -p cmd internal pkg
  cat > cmd/main.go <<'EOF'
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    fmt.Println("Hello, Go!")
}
EOF
  cat > README.md <<EOF
